  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 111 AM CDT Sun Nov 1 2026\n\nAs of 1 AM temperatures across the region are in the 40s with winds \nout of the south at around 10 mph. Some light showers or drizzle \nwill continue this morning across eastern SD with little to no \naccumulation expected. Today will be the warmest day for the \nforecast period across most areas with highs in the 60s. Winds this \nafternoon will be out of the south and gust between 25 and 30 mph \nmainly west of the James River.\n\nThe main focus of the forecast is still the precipitation starting \nlate Sunday and lasting through Tuesday as a low pressure system \nmakes its way across the forecast area. We still see widespread \nchances above 60% from late Sunday evening through early Tuesday \nmorning, with chances coming to an end west to east during the day \nTuesday. The chance for more than one inch between Monday and \nTuesday mornings is between 75 and 95% for areas along and east of \nthe Missouri River, only slightly less west. The chance for more \nthan 2 inches in that same time frame has come down considerably and \nis now between 45 and 65% mainly east of the James River. The chance \nfor more than 2 inches between Sunday night and Tuesday night (48 \nhours) is 55 to 80% mainly around and east of the Missouri River, \n45% or less to the west. \n\nThe cold front associated with that incoming low will make its way \nfrom northwest to southeast across the area Monday resulting in much \ncooler highs for north central SD, generally in the upper 50s, and a \nbit warmer for everyone else, generally in the low 60s. Much cooler \nair will move in behind the cold front and low, bringing our \ntemperatures down to around normal, or highs in the upper 40s to low \n50s. Winds are still looking to be strong with this incoming low \nwith gusts of 35 to 40 mph spreading from west to east through the \nday Monday and into Tuesday. Winds of 45 to 55 mph will be possible \nalong and west of the Missouri River. These higher end gusts will \nslowly come to an end through the day Tuesday.",
